    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for elementwise tensor multiplication. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradMultiply" kindref="compound">GradMultiply</ref> class represents the elementwise multiplication operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for the Hadamard product of two tensors. For the operation <formula id="51">$C = A \odot B$</formula> where <formula id="52">$\odot$</formula> denotes elementwise multiplication, the gradient computation follows from the derivatives:    <formula id="53">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = B, \quad \frac{\partial C}{\partial B}
= A
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is multiplied elementwise with the appropriate saved tensor according to the chain rule:    <formula id="54">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot B
\]</formula>    <formula id="55">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial B} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial B} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot A
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves copies of both input tensors as they are required to compute the gradients with respect to each input during the backward pass.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradMultiplyScalar" kindref="compound">GradMultiplyScalar</ref> for the gradient function for tensor-scalar multiplication. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradMultiplyMatrix" kindref="compound">GradMultiplyMatrix</ref> for the gradient function for matrix multiplication. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
